    <screens>
        <name>Price_Objections</name>
        <label>Price Objections</label>
        <locationX>799</locationX>
        <locationY>196</locationY>
        <allowBack>true</allowBack>
        <allowFinish>true</allowFinish>
        <allowPause>true</allowPause>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Process_Objections</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <fields>
            <name>PObjectionHandling</name>
            <fieldText>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;color: black; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Price Objection Handling&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;One thing we can do is adjust the benefit amount to reduce the price. Do you have a certain budget in mind that you want to stick to?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;[rerun quote as needed]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;[reason for FE vs. Term] Well one thing to keep in mind is that you don’t want to outlive your coverage. Term insurance can be a cheaper in some cases, but it only lasts a specific period of time, and if – WHEN! – you outlive it you’ll need to get a new policy which will probably be much more expensive because you’ll be older.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;[reason2 for FE vs. Term] Term insurance can be a great product for a lot of people – we often use it to cover people during their working years or when they have young children. Since you’re &amp;lt;age appropriate comment, like “retired” not “older”&amp;gt; and your needs are a different now we want coverage that will be there for you no matter how long you live. It might be a little more expensive or provide a different benefit amount, but this kind of product is more in-line with what you need. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;[reason for FE vs. “whole life”] This product is actually a type of whole life product just like you’re thinking! It’s just designed with a simple application process and reasonably priced for people who want coverage for when they pass away.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</fieldText>
            <fieldType>DisplayText</fieldType>
            <styleProperties>
                <verticalAlignment>
                    <stringValue>top</stringValue>
                </verticalAlignment>
                <width>
                    <stringValue>12</stringValue>
                </width>
            </styleProperties>
        </fields>
        <showFooter>true</showFooter>
        <showHeader>false</showHeader>
    </screens>
    <screens>
        <name>Process_Objections</name>
        <label>Process Objections</label>
        <locationX>675</locationX>
        <locationY>196</locationY>
        <allowBack>true</allowBack>
        <allowFinish>true</allowFinish>
        <allowPause>true</allowPause>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>PreQual_Knockouts</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <fields>
            <name>ProcessObjections</name>
            <fieldText>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;color: black; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Process issues/reasons&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;One thing that often frustrates people about Life Insurance is the application process. It can take a long time, tons of paperwork, and some companies require you to do a medical exam, or look at your medical records. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;We really like this product because it eliminates a bunch of that! We do a quick online application, we find out if you’re approved immediately and your coverage can be in place today – we can get it all done right now in about 20 minutes!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;[if/once yes] Great! Lets start the application and see if we can get this knocked out right now! Here’s how it works, I’ll pull up their application online and go through it asking you some additional questions about your health and lifestyle. It will take us about 20 minutes, and at the end they’ll tell us if you’re approved and you’ll have a policy!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;One thing to remember, because we’re applying for life insurance – there are some personal questions that the insurance company requires, but keep in mind, your personal information is completely confidential and won’t be shared with anyone besides us and the insurance company.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</fieldText>
            <fieldType>DisplayText</fieldType>
            <styleProperties>
                <verticalAlignment>
                    <stringValue>top</stringValue>
                </verticalAlignment>
                <width>
                    <stringValue>12</stringValue>
                </width>
            </styleProperties>
        </fields>
        <showFooter>true</showFooter>
        <showHeader>false</showHeader>
    </screens>
    <screens>
        <name>Step_1</name>
        <label>Step 1</label>
        <locationX>216</locationX>
        <locationY>47</locationY>
        <allowBack>false</allowBack>
        <allowFinish>true</allowFinish>
        <allowPause>false</allowPause>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Step_2</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <fields>
            <name>Text1</name>
            <fieldText>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Step 1: Intro&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px; color: black;&quot;&gt;Hi &amp;lt;CLIENT NAME&amp;gt;! Thanks for holding, my name is &amp;lt;AGENT&amp;gt; I’m a Senior Licensed Agent with Sage Insurance and I’m here to help you get that coverage that you’re looking for. Just to let you know we’re on a recorded line. Do you currently have life insurance?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px; color: black;&quot;&gt;[If Yes] That’s great, are you looking to increase that coverage or compare it? &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-family: sans-serif; color: black;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Did you get that coverage recently?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-family: sans-serif; color: black;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-family: sans-serif; color: black;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;[if Yes] How was that experience? Were you approved?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-family: sans-serif; color: black;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;[use response to talk about our easy process lead into Step 2]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-family: sans-serif; color: black;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-family: sans-serif; color: black;&quot;&gt;[if Declined – Clarify] You were declined for life, health, or disability insurance? [KO, if yes]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-family: sans-serif; color: black;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-family: sans-serif; color: black;&quot;&gt;[If Replacing] Unfortunately we can’t help with policy replacements at this time. [KO, if yes]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-family: sans-serif; color: black;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-family: sans-serif; color: black;&quot;&gt;[If No] Great!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</fieldText>
            <fieldType>DisplayText</fieldType>
            <styleProperties>
                <verticalAlignment>
                    <stringValue>top</stringValue>
                </verticalAlignment>
                <width>
                    <stringValue>12</stringValue>
                </width>
            </styleProperties>
        </fields>
        <fields>
            <name>Agent_Notes</name>
            <dataType>String</dataType>
            <fieldText>Agent Notes</fieldText>
            <fieldType>InputField</fieldType>
            <isRequired>false</isRequired>
            <styleProperties>
                <verticalAlignment>
                    <stringValue>top</stringValue>
                </verticalAlignment>
                <width>
                    <stringValue>12</stringValue>
                </width>
            </styleProperties>
        </fields>
        <showFooter>true</showFooter>
        <showHeader>false</showHeader>
    </screens>
    <screens>
        <name>Step_2</name>
        <label>Step 2</label>
        <locationX>333</locationX>
        <locationY>47</locationY>
        <allowBack>true</allowBack>
        <allowFinish>true</allowFinish>
        <allowPause>true</allowPause>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Step_3</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <fields>
            <name>Step2</name>
            <fieldText>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-family: sans-serif; color: black;&quot;&gt;Step 2: Explain the Process, Set Expectations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-family: sans-serif; color: black;&quot;&gt;Sage is part of one of the largest insurance marketplaces in the US, based just outside of Boston. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-family: sans-serif; color: black;&quot;&gt;[Lumico statement] We work with Lumico Insurance Company they’ve &lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-family: sans-serif; color: black; background-color: yellow;&quot;&gt;insured over 1m people in US&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-family: sans-serif; color: black;&quot;&gt;I’m going to take you through our system to build you a personalized plan to fit your needs and budget. Our process designed to save you time and money. Again, my name is &amp;lt;AGENT NAME&amp;gt;, I help clients all across the country and I’ll do my best to make this fast and easy for you.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-family: sans-serif; color: black;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-family: sans-serif; color: black;&quot;&gt;First, I want to take a little time to understand your situation; who are you looking to protect with this coverage?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</fieldText>
            <fieldType>DisplayText</fieldType>
            <styleProperties>
                <verticalAlignment>
                    <stringValue>top</stringValue>
                </verticalAlignment>
                <width>
                    <stringValue>12</stringValue>
                </width>
            </styleProperties>
        </fields>
